8661  0.07632804]\n"," [0.7258661  1.0000001  0.0169613 ]\n"," [0.07632804 0.0169613  1.        ]]\n"]}],"source":["sentences2 = [\n","    \"How can I develop an AI application?\",\n","    \"How do I build an artificial intelligence system?\",\n","    \"What is the capital of Bangladesh?\",\n","]\n","\n","# Generate embeddings\n","embeddings2 = model.encode(sentences2)\n","\n","# Calculate cosine similarity\n","similarity2 = cosine_similarity(embeddings2)\n","\n","print(similarity2)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"65f62ff5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.343377Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.343003Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.54957Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.548554Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.214327,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.551736+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.337409+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x500 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n","\n","plt.bar(range(50), embedding2[:50])\n","\n","plt.xlabel(\"Embedding Dimensions\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Vector Values\")\n","plt.title(\"Visualization of First 50 Embedding Dimensions\")\n","\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"aeaa6c9a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004917,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.561612+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.556695+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Vector Database\n","\n","When you generate embeddings, you typically store them in a database along with the original sentence.\n","\n","Each sentence gets converted into a numerical vector by your embedding model.\n","\n","The database stores three important things:\n","\n","1. ID: Unique identifier for each sentence.\n","2. Text: Original sentence.\n","3. Embedding: Numerical vector generated by the embedding model.\n","\n","### How data looks in a database\n","\n","| id | sentence                               | embedding                 |\n","| -- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n","| 1  | I love machine learning                | `[0.21, 0.45, 0.78, ...]` |\n","| 2  | Python is a programming language       | `[0.32, 0.12, 0.89, ...]` |\n","| 3  | Artificial intelligence is fascinating | `[0.56, 0.23, 0.67, ...]` |\n","\n","The embedding column stores the entire vector (for example, 384 floating-point values), not just the first and last five values.\n","\n","### Store embeddings using SQLite\n","\n","SQLite is a simple database that you can use to understand how embedding storage works.\n","\n","```py\n","import sqlite3\n","import json\n","\n","# Connect to database\n","conn = sqlite3.connect(\"embeddings.db\")\n","cursor = conn.cursor()\n","\n","# Create table\n","cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sentences (\n","    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n","    sentence TEXT,\n","    embedding TEXT\n",")\n","\"\"\")\n","\n","# Generate and store embeddings\n","for sentence in sentences:\n","\n","    embedding = model.encode(sentence)\n","\n","    cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n","        INSERT INTO sentences (sentence, embedding)\n","        VALUES (?, ?)\n","    \"\"\", (\n","        sentence,\n","        json.dumps(embedding.tolist())\n","    ))\n","\n","conn.commit()\n","conn.close()\n","\n","print(\"Embeddings stored successfully!\")\n","```\n","\n","Here:\n","\n","- `sentence` stores the original text.\n","- `embedding` stores the vector as a JSON string.\n","- `embedding.tolist()` converts the NumPy array into a Python list.\n","- `json.dumps()` converts that list into a string for SQLite storage.\n","\n","### Retrieve embeddings from the database\n","\n","Now let's retrieve the stored vectors.\n","\n","```py\n","import sqlite3\n","import json\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","conn = sqlite3.connect(\"embeddings.db\")\n","cursor = conn.cursor()\n","\n","cursor.execute(\"SELECT * FROM sentences\")\n","\n","rows = cursor.fetchall()\n","\n","for row in rows:\n","\n","    id = row[0]\n","    sentence = row[1]\n","    embedding = np.array(json.loads(row[2]))\n","\n","    print(f\"\\nID: {id}\")\n","    print(f\"Sentence: {sentence}\")\n","    print(f\"Embedding dimensions: {len(embedding)}\")\n","    print(f\"First 5 values: {embedding[:5]}\")\n","\n","conn.close()\n","```\n","\n","### What exactly does a vector database store?\n","\n","A vector database typically stores more than just vectors.\n","\n","It stores three important things:\n","\n","1. Vector embeddings.\n","2. Original data or a reference to the original data.\n","3. Metadata.\n","\n","For example, imagine you are building a RAG application for technical documentation.\n","\n","A record might look like this:\n","\n","```py\n","{\n","    \"id\": \"doc_001\",\n","    \"text\": \"FastAPI is a Python web framework.\",\n","    \"embedding\": [\n","        0.21,\n","        0.45,\n","        0.78,\n","        0.12\n","    ],\n","    \"metadata\": {\n","        \"source\": \"fastapi_documentation.pdf\",\n","        \"page\": 12,\n","        \"category\": \"programming\",\n","        \"author\": \"OpenAI\"\n","    }\n","}\n","```\n","\n","The embedding above is illustrative, not an actual embedding.\n","\n","Let's understand each field.\n","\n","| Field     | Purpose                              |\n","| --------- | ------------------------------------ |\n","| ID        | Uniquely identifies a record         |\n","| Text      | Original content                     |\n","| Embedding | Numerical representation             |\n","| Metadata  | Additional information for filtering |\n","\n","**Why store metadata?**\n","\n","Imagine a user asks:\n","\n","> Explain FastAPI authentication from the official documentation.\n","\n","You can search semantically while filtering:\n","\n","```py\n","filter = {    \n","    \"category\": \"programming\",\n","    \"source\": \"fastapi_documentation.pdf\"\n","}\n","```\n","\n","This allows you to combine semantic search with traditional filtering.\n","\n","### What database should you use in real projects?\n","\n","SQLite is fine for learning, but production semantic search systems commonly use vector databases.\n","\n","| Database              | Purpose                                |\n","| --------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n","| SQLite                | Basic embedding storage                |\n","| PostgreSQL + pgvector | Relational database with vector search |\n","| FAISS                 | Fast similarity search                 |\n","| ChromaDB              | Developer-friendly vector database     |\n","| Pinecone              | Managed vector database                |\n","\n","## Similarity Searching\n","\n","This is probably the most important mathematical concept behind vector databases.\n","\n","When you search for something, the database needs to determine which stored vectors are closest to your query vector.\n","\n","There are several similarity and distance metrics.\n","\n","The three most important are:\n","\n","1. Cosine similarity\n","2. Euclidean distance (L2)\n","3. Dot product (inner product)\n","\n","Let's understand each one.\n","\n","### Cosine similarity\n","\n","Cosine similarity measures the angle between two vectors.\n","\n","It tells us how similar the directions of two vectors are.\n","\n","The formula is:\n","\n","$$ \\text{Cosine Similarity}(A,B)= \\frac{A\\cdot B}{||A||\\\\,||B||} $$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","- $A$ = Query vector.\n","- $B$ = Stored vector.\n","- $A\\cdot B$ = Dot product.\n","- $||A||$ = Magnitude (length) of vector A.\n","- $||B||$ = Magnitude of vector B.\n","\n","Let's use a simple example.\n","\n","Suppose:\n","\n","$$ A=[1,2] $$\n","\n","$$ B=[2,4] $$\n","\n","First, calculate the dot product:\n","\n","$$ A\\cdot B=(1\\times2)+(2\\times4) $$\n","\n","$$ =2+8=10 $$\n","\n","Calculate the magnitude of A:\n","\n","$$ ||A||=\\sqrt{1^2+2^2} =\\sqrt{5} $$\n","\n","Calculate the magnitude of B:\n","\n","$$ ||B||=\\sqrt{2^2+4^2} =\\sqrt{20} $$\n","\n","Now:\n","\n","$$ \\text{Similarity}= \\frac{10}{\\sqrt5\\times\\sqrt{20}} $$\n","\n","$$ =\\frac{10}{10}=1 $$\n","\n","Similarity = 1.0\n","\n","This means the vectors have exactly the same direction.\n","\n","#### Understanding cosine similarity values\n","\n","| Score | General interpretation     |\n","| ----- | -------------------------- |\n","| 1     | Same direction             |\n","| 0.9   | Very similar direction     |\n","| 0.7   | Somewhat similar direction |\n","| 0     | Perpendicular directions   |\n","| -1    | Opposite directions        |\n","\n","These are geometric interpretations, not universal semantic similarity thresholds. The meaning of a score depends on the embedding model and dataset."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"id":"a57cedd0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.572495Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.572088Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.57866Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.577357Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.014988,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.581096+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.566108+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["0.72586596\n"]}],"source":["similarity3 = np.dot(embeddings2[0], embeddings2[1]) / (np.linalg.norm(embeddings2[0]) * np.linalg.norm(embeddings2[1]))\n","\n","print(similarity3)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"4c978e1d","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005078,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.591383+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.586305+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**When is cosine similarity useful?**\n","\n","- Semantic search.\n","- Document retrieval.\n","- RAG applications.\n","- Text similarity.\n","- Recommendation systems.\n","\n","It is particularly useful when vector direction matters more than vector magnitude.\n","\n","### Euclidean distance (L2 distance)\n","\n","Euclidean distance measures the straight-line distance between two points in vector space.\n","\n","Formula:\n","\n","$$ d(A,B)=\\sqrt{\\sum\\_{i=1}^{n}(A_i-B_i)^2} $$\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","$$ A=[1,2] $$\n","\n","$$ B=[4,6] $$\n","\n","Calculate:\n","\n","$$ d(A,B)=\\sqrt{(1-4)^2+(2-6)^2} $$\n","\n","$$ =\\sqrt{9+16} $$\n","\n","$$ =\\sqrt{25}=5 $$\n","\n","Distance = 5\n","\n","Unlike cosine similarity:\n","\n","- Smaller distance means more similar.\n","- Larger distance means less similar."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"id":"5ccc66fe","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.602298Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.601891Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.607646Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.606564Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.013827,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.609831+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.596004+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["0.7404513\n"]}],"source":["distance = np.linalg.norm(embeddings2[0] - embeddings2[1])\n","\n","print(distance)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1a9b99c9","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004594,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.619262+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.614668+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**When is Euclidean distance useful?**\n","\n","- Image similarity.\n","- Spatial data.\n","- Clustering.\n","- Some recommendation systems.\n","- Embedding models trained with distance-based objectives.\n","\n","### Dot product (inner product)\n","\n","Dot product multiplies corresponding vector dimensions and sums the results.\n","\n","Formula:\n","\n","$$ A\\cdot B=\\sum\\_{i=1}^{n} A_iB_i $$\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","$$ A=[1,2,3] $$\n","\n","$$ B=[4,5,6] $$\n","\n","$$ A\\cdot B=(1\\times4)+(2\\times5)+(3\\times6) $$\n","\n","$$ =4+10+18=32 $$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":15,"id":"a7588fa1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.63016Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.629736Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.635436Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.634374Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.013616,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.637507+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.623891+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["0.7258659\n"]}],"source":["result = np.dot(embeddings2[0], embeddings2[1])\n","\n","print(result)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ee474b14","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004693,"end_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.64687+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-31T10:04:10.642177+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Dot product considers both direction and magnitude.\n","\n","It is often used when the embedding model and retrieval setup are designed for inner-product search.\n","\n","### Comparison of similarity algorithms\n","\n","| Metric             | What it measures        | Best score |\n","| ------------------ | ----------------------- | ---------- |\n","| Cosine similarity  | Direction similarity    | Higher     |\n","| Euclidean distance | Straight-line distance  | Lower      |\n","| Dot product        | Direction and magnitude | Higher     |\n","\n","Important production consideration:\n","\n","You should choose the metric according to the embedding model's training and retrieval recommendations.\n","\n","For normalized vectors, cosine similarity and dot product produce equivalent rankings because the vector magnitudes are 1.\n","\n","Likewise, for unit-normalized vectors:\n","\n","$$\n","||A-B||^2=2-2(A\\cdot B)\n","$$\n","\n","This means maximizing cosine similarity, maximizing dot product, and minimizing square